<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pasig River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pasig River flows from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laguna-de-bay">Laguna de Bay</a> through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> to Manila Bay in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>. Its delta was home to the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagalog-language">Tagalog</a> polities of Tondo on the north bank, Maynila on the south bank and Namayan upstream, which traded with Chinese and Bornean merchants. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> made Manila its capital after taking it in 1571.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pasig-river.jpg" alt="Pasig River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: patrickroque01 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pasig_River,_Quiapo_(Manila)(2019-01-09).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
